From 4c3283449578d0e558e6065dcc8451a3684a7f5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 08:22:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [Channel Planning]: CBS retry on driver unavailability and
 wsc completion

1. Fixed issue with CBS not re-triggering for a pre-defined retries
   if the resource is busy.
  * CBS-STARTED is emitted unconditionally before the driver call, so it is
    NOT a success signal.
  * When driver->set_cbs() returns -EBUSY, hostapd -- in the SAME synchronous
    call -- clears cbs_enable, emits CBS-ABORTED, and returns the error, so
    the 'CBS enable 1' wpa_ctrl reply is FAIL. CBS-ABORTED and the FAIL reply
    are the same synchronous, per-link event.
  * hostapd does not self-retry on -EBUSY.
  * Real completion is the later CBS-COMPLETE event.

    Fix: retry inside ap_wlan_hal_nl80211::trigger_cbs(), keyed on the
         synchronous 'CBS enable 1' FAIL (== per-link Resource busy / CBS-ABORTED).
    The retry is:
    * Per-radio/per-link contained (m_radio_info.iface_name control socket),
      so only the busy link is re-issued;
    * Bounded by CBS_TRIGGER_MAX_ABORT_RETRIES (default 3) with a
      CBS_TRIGGER_RETRY_SETTLE_MS (default 500ms) delay to let the driver's
      abort/cleanup settle before re-issuing;
    * Free of any completion timeout, so a valid slow 6GHz CBS scan (>1 min)
      that returns OK synchronously is never misread as a failure.

2. In dedicated Agent configuration scenarios, make use of the
   Autoconfiguration task's complete indication to trigger a one-time
   "CBS" trigger for all applicable radios.

3. When no positive rank is generated for a radio(parsed from driver rank),
   instead of reporting the preference in the preference table as "1", when
   standard channel selction path is not enabled, repot it as "14".

No functional change when CBS is disabled: trigger_cbs() is only reached
when cbs_based_chansel_enable or chansel_preference_report_refresh_enable
is set.

Files:
  common/beerocks/bwl/nl80211/ap_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp
  agent/src/beerocks/slave/tasks/channel_selection_task.h
  agent/src/beerocks/slave/tasks/channel_selection_task.cpp

Signed-off-by: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
